  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b769da97cc9c62c4c9115b0b03ad86d2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dad's Journal
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  pages:
  - "Journal Entry 1:\n\nIt was supposed to be an apology. I\u2019ve been driving
    back and forth on those dark highway roads every night, coming home long after
    my dear boys are asleep. My business is drowning. If I lose it, we lose all of
    this: the house, the peaceful countryside, the life I nearly broke my back to
    give them. I bought the doll from a small stall on the side of the road. An innocent
    gift for Sammy to make up for all the late nights. I had no idea what I was bringing
    across our threshold. Anne has been trying to hold us together, but I hear her
    crying in the hallway when she thinks I\u2019m asleep. She sits up until dawn
    reading the Bible, refusing to touch the sleeping pills I brought home. So I
    started taking them instead. Copious amounts just to shut my brain off for an
    hour or two, washing them down with a drink. I even picked up smoking again after
    six years clean. My hands won't stop shaking."
  - 'Journal Entry 2:


    I haven''t reached out to Miguel about what is happening.
    I can''t bring myself to involve him, terrified that this thing will latch onto
    my eldest son too. This curse stays with me. I went back for the salesman instead.
    I lost my mind and beat the man to a bloody pulp in his own shop, screaming at
    him to take it back. Through the blood, he swore he couldn''t undo it, but he
    gave me the ritual. Banishment requires the entire home''s power system running
    at full strength while a concentrated red flash is fired directly at the doll
    in the center of the house. The light keeps it at bay. But every time I try,
    it snaps the breaker box and breaks the main lever right off to ensure the lights
    stay dead.'
  - "Journal Entry 3:\n\nI managed to source a spare breaker lever and secured it
    inside a locked tool box nearby. I was planning to make one final attempt tonight.
    I misplaced the note where I wrote down the combination, but that doesn't matter,
    the numbers are burned into my memory anyway. The problem is no matter where
    I hide that grotesque piece of wood and cloth, whether locked in the shed or
    thrown under the garage workbench, it always finds its way back into Sammy\u2019s
    room. Over the last two days, its behavior has turned wildly erratic. Door handles
    rattle on their own, the temperature plunges, and the shadows in the hallways
    stretch toward us when we turn our backs."
  - "Journal Entry 4:\n\nWe can\u2019t fight this anymore. We are packing whatever
    fits in the trunk of the car tonight and running. Let it keep the house. Let
    it keep everything I worked for. I just need my wife and my sons alive. "
  triggersObjective: 0
